<title>FINLAND: Finnish PM Lipponen repeats that EMU is on track.</title>
<headline>Finnish PM Lipponen repeats that EMU is on track.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish Prime Minister Paavo Lipponen on Monday repeated that the process towards Europe's new single currency was on track.</p>
<p>&quot;Passage to the third stage of economic and monetary union is on track as the Amsterdam meeting confirmed the stability and growth pact,&quot; Lipponen said in the text of a prepared speech.</p>
<p>He was referring to the June 16-17 summit of European Union heads of state and government in Amsterdam.</p>
<p>&quot;Decisions in Amsterdam make clear that securing economic growth and the creation of new jobs are among the priorities for the Union,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
